# oracle: fix colvars (COLVARS package, the Colvars library) on a 256-atom LJ liquid of two masses: a distance between two weighted centres of mass (width 0.5), a distanceVec across the periodic boundary, a cartesian component with useZ off and outputAppliedForce, a polynomial combination (componentCoeff 0.5, componentExp 2 with a dummyAtom group and forceNoPBC, plus a second distance), two harmonic restraints (outputEnergy, a default name harmonic2, vector centers), fix_modify energy yes, two runs with the traj every 5 steps and the state every 20; thermo with f_ID and f_ID[i][j], the traj and state files compared
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native: thermo 6.9e-15 (pe and etotal, from the pair sum order; every f_2 column is equal at %.15g), final atoms 1.3e-13, state files byte-identical, traj 1e-15 after step 40.
# oracle-inputs: w762cv_lj.colvars
# oracle-files: ljcv.colvars.traj ljcv.colvars.state
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 filerel=1e-10
units           lj
atom_modify     map array
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
set             atom 1*128 type 2
mass            1 1.0
mass            2 2.5
velocity        all create 1.5 87287 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all colvars w762cv_lj.colvars output ljcv
fix_modify      2 energy yes
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal f_2 f_2[1][1] f_2[2][1] f_2[2][2] f_2[2][3] f_2[3][1] f_2[3][4] f_2[4][1]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             50
run             30
